    {
      "id": "ideas",
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Three patterns to recognise",
      "points": [
        "**Two pointers**: on sorted data, move pointers from both ends inward. Pair sums, palindromes: **O(n)**.",
        "**Sliding window**: for \"best subarray of size k\", slide a window, adding the new item and removing the old: **O(n)**.",
        "**Frequency map**: for counting or \"have I seen this?\", use a HashMap or HashSet (see Hashing).",
        "Read the problem for clues: *sorted*, *pair*, *subarray*, *consecutive*, *count*."
      ],
      "pattern": "window += a[i] - a[i - k]; // slide: add the new, drop the old\nbest = Math.max(best, window);"
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "type": "predict",
      "prompt": "A classic trap. What does this print?",
      "code": "public class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        int[] a = {2, 1, 5, 1, 3, 2};\n        int k = 3, window = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) window += a[i];\n        int best = window;\n        for (int i = k; i < a.length; i++) {\n            window += a[i] - a[i - k];\n            best = Math.max(best, window);\n        }\n        System.out.println(best);\n    }\n}",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "9",
          "why": "Yes. The windows sum to 8, 7, 9 and 6, and the best is 9."
        },
        {
          "text": "8",
          "why": "That’s only the first window (2 + 1 + 5). The window slides on and finds 5 + 1 + 3 = 9."
        },
        {
          "text": "6",
          "why": "That’s the last window. best keeps the maximum seen."
        },
        {
          "text": "14",
          "why": "That’s the whole array. The window is only k = 3 wide."
        }
      ],
      "answer": 0
    },
